 1. unless 1 > 2 ... else ... end            -> "body"
 2. unless ... elsif ... end                 -> SyntaxError
 3. n = 0; until n >= 4 ... n += 1           -> 4
 4. r << x if c; r << y unless c             -> ["if", "unless"]
 5. n = 10; n += 1 while n < 3               -> 10  (tested first, never ran)
 6. n = 10; begin n += 1 end while n < 3     -> 11  (ran once, then tested)
 7. loop do ... break i * 10 ... end         -> 30
 8. if/elsif/else/end                        -> compiles
 9. if ... elif true ... end                 -> compiles; when that branch runs: NoMethodError
10. else if ... with one end / two ends      -> SyntaxError / compiles
11. y = 5 if false; then y                   -> nil  (defined? -> "local-variable")
12. for ... else (search with no hit)        -> SyntaxError; find -> 9 / nil
